    "title": "2026 Final Four TV schedule, tip times for today’s games on April 4",
    "text": "The 2026 NCAA Tournament is winding down, with the Final Four set to tip off on Saturday, April 4, at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis, as we determine who will be playing in the national championship game.After a thrilling Final Four in the women’s tournament on Friday night, the men have a lot to live up to.AdvertisementSaturday’s Final Four action will get underway at 6:09 p.m. ET, with the No. 2 UConn Huskies facing off against the No. 3-seeded Illinois Fighting Illini, who are the lowest-remaining seed in the tournament field.WATCH: Dawn Staley, Geno Auriemma have heated altercation in tense Final Four battleIn the nightcap, the remaining two No. 1 seeds will go head-to-head, with the Michigan Wolverines facing off against the Arizona Wildcats.Both games will air on TBS, truTV, and HBO Max.When will your favorite team or national championship pick be taking the court on Saturday night?A full look at the TV schedule for the Final Four can be seen below (all times Eastern).AdvertisementWATCH: Geno Auriemma crashes out during UConn’s Final Four shockerFinal Four – Saturday, April 4(2) UConn vs. (3) Illinois, 6:09 p.m. | TBS/TNT/truTV(1) Michigan vs. (1) Arizona, ~9 p.m. (Tip-off will be approximately 30 minutes after the conclusion of the first game) | TBS/TNT/truTVNational Championship – Monday, April 6TBD vs. TBD, 8:30 p.m. ET— Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead —",
